ness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. So `2.665` rounded to `2.67` and failed the test, which expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under policy, so that step is still open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test file.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Gdvb58JTv2DwbqstxkA9tL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NyLA5EikqPxmqiumN7eMKj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 require `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under half-up, `2.665` rounds to `2.67`, which fails the test's second assertion. I'll create a branch and make the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GNq1svrC71V2ky5Y1dMnt5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MEL6hSN26oo9fCkLEnvJv7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN for round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money documented banker's rounding but used ROUND_HALF_UP, so\ntests/test_money.py fails (2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Commit is on the branch. Next I'll start CI against it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LBFA9W27muQsEC6DN7meZA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011mnxFnU932LDUJkJKVAUNd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. I'll open the pull request against main and request alex as reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YR5gT4LdNf5eFbrQDeMx1k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` is documented as using banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it was implemented with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (`2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in `src/money.py`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. So `2.665` rounded to `2.67` and failed the test, which expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under policy, so that step is still open.", "type": "text"}]}]}